{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy by design privacy by design","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md","fileName":"Privacy by Design.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy by Design","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Governance and Responsible Innovation]], [[Big Data Governance and Quality]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Governance and Responsible Innovation","Big Data Governance and Quality","Meaningful Digital Consent","aiethics.epub","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy by design privacy by design","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md","fileName":"Privacy by Design.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy by Design","heading":"Privacy by Design","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Privacy by design makes privacy a requirement throughout the engineering process rather than a feature added after data practices are fixed. It can influence collection limits, default settings, access control, retention, combination, user information, and the ability to erase or correct data.\n\nThe approach is especially important for AI because models often depend on large datasets and may infer information beyond what was directly supplied. General commitments must be translated into concrete decisions about purpose and risk. [[Meaningful Digital Consent]] remains important, but privacy-preserving defaults reduce the burden placed on individuals to understand every technical consequence.\n\nKelleher and Tierney use children's free-to-play games with third-party advertising to show why privacy cannot be delegated to a downstream provider or considered only after launch. Designers must inspect the users, the records shared with advertising networks, and the content those networks return. Privacy by design makes those consequences part of the system's initial architecture and organizational practice.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Governance and Responsible Innovation","Big Data Governance and Quality","Meaningful Digital Consent","aiethics.epub","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy by design privacy by design","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy by Design.md","fileName":"Privacy by Design.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy by Design","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]\n\n[[bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf]]\n\n[[datascience_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Governance and Responsible Innovation","Big Data Governance and Quality","Meaningful Digital Consent","aiethics.epub","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}